{"finish_reason":"stop","kind":"response","reasoning":"What was changed this turn: `touch docs/missing.md && python3 linkcheck.py; echo \"exit=$?\"; rm docs/missing.md` — I created `docs/missing.md` and re-ran, then deleted it.\n\nWhat did this change establish? That when there are no broken links, the script exits with exit code 0 (the success path) — it established that the exit-0 path works.\n\nWhat did it depend on being true? That `docs/missing.md` was the only broken link (i.e., all other links resolve), and that the link-check regex / existence check treats a newly created empty file as existing. Also depends on `python3` being available and the script being correct as before.\n\nFields: LEARNED, EVIDENCE, STUCK, one per line, NONE if nothing to record.\n\nLEARNED: when no broken links exist, the checker exits with exit code 0 (success path verified).\nEVIDENCE: the run produced no output and `exit=0`.\nSTUCK: none — nothing blocking. Probably NONE.\n\nFormat: three lines, \"LEARNED: ...\", \"EVIDENCE: ...\", \"STUCK: ...\". Keep it concise.\n","seq":1160,"t":50268,"text":"\n\nLEARNED: The checker's success path is verified — with no broken links it prints nothing and exits 0 (the `missing.md` target counts as existing as soon as the file is present, since the check is a plain existence test).\nEVIDENCE: The run output was empty except `exit=0`, immediately after `touch docs/missing.md` and before `rm` restored the broken state.\nSTUCK: NONE","timings":{"cache_n":4096,"draft_n":805,"draft_n_accepted":238,"predicted_ms":4059.9999999999995,"predicted_n":353,"prompt_ms":310.0,"prompt_n":218},"to_request":1043,"usage":{"cached_tokens":4096,"completion_tokens":353,"prompt_tokens":4314}}
