{"ask":"judgment","at":1548,"hazard":"may-displace-trunk-cache","kind":"fork","lane":"interview","of_turn":2,"question":"Answer from this turn alone.\nThe working record so far, one entry per line as its id, a tab, then the entry:\ninterview-t1-0\tlearned: The checker's success path works — with every local link resolving it prints nothing and exits 0 — and the docs tree contained no other broken links, i.e. the fence-skip and external-scheme-skip logic produced no false positives on the fake in-fence link and the https link.\ninterview-t1-1\tevidence: The run printed only `exit=0` after `touch docs/missing.md`; this depended on the prior run having reported exactly one broken link (`docs/index.md:4: missing.md`) and on `check_file`'s anchor/external/fence skips being correct, since any of those failing would have added report lines and broken the exit-0 result.\ninterview-t1-f1042-0\tlearned: The checker's success path is verified — with no broken links it prints nothing and exits 0 (the `missing.md` target counts as existing as soon as the file is present, since the check is a plain existence test).\ninterview-t1-f1042-1\tevidence: The run output was empty except `exit=0`, immediately after `touch docs/missing.md` and before `rm` restored the broken state.\ninterview-t1-f1164-0\tlearned: linkcheck.py detects the seeded broken link, prints it as `file:line: target`, exits 1 when broken links exist, and exits 0 when the target file exists (also correctly ignoring external links and fenced code).\ninterview-t1-f1164-1\tevidence: first run printed `docs/index.md:4: missing.md` with `exit=1`; after `touch docs/missing.md` the second run printed nothing with `exit=0`.\ninterview-t1-f1366-0\tdecision: The task is complete — `linkcheck.py` (stdlib-only, fence-aware, skips anchors/external schemes) and three sample files in `docs/` were created; the single run reported `docs/index.md:4: missing.md` with exit 1, and the success path (exit 0) was verified with a temporary file, so the deliverable stands as-is.\ninterview-t1-f1366-1\tplan: Nothing further is intended; no follow-up steps unless the user requests changes (e.g., new options, CI integration, or additional fixtures).\ninterview-t1-f696-0\tlearned: linkcheck.py's success path works — it exits 0 when every local link resolves, and the broken `missing.md` link at docs/index.md:4 was the only broken link in docs/ (fenced code, external, and anchor links were all correctly ignored).\ninterview-t1-f696-1\tevidence: With `touch docs/missing.md` in place, the run printed only `exit=0`; the identical run without it had printed `docs/index.md:4: missing.md` and `exit=1` — the only difference between the two runs was the file's existence.\nThe turn has ended. What did you decide, and what do you intend next? Answer with the fields DECISION, PLAN and SUPERSEDE, one per line. SUPERSEDE cites the id of a working-record entry this turn replaces, then the entry that should stand; write NONE for a field with nothing to record.\n","seq":2053,"t":85372,"trigger":"turn_end","view":"last_turn","why":"scoping"}
